ills than those learnt at school or work.\\nFor information related to the exam process itself,\\nUCD Assessment\\nis the best place to go for up-to-date information, including how to access your timetable, how to get to the exam centres, and the procedures in place during exams. You will also find useful information on your exam results at this link.\\nPreparing for exams\\nIf you would like some tips on how to improve your study skills and exam techniques then you may find our\\nguide on\\nAcademic Support\\nhelpful\\n.\\nIf you have questions related to your exam or module content, please contact your module coordinator(s).\\nCoping with exam stress\\n\\n---\\n[File: academic_regulations_2025_26.md > **ACADEMIC REGULATIONS 2025-2026** >> Contents]\\nContent: |**Professional**<br>**Accreditation**|The University is responsible for the design and validation of its own degree<br>programmes. Where those programmes are also subject to professional|  \\n9  \\n---  \\n###### Page 10 of 84  \\n||accreditation,<br>the requireme<br>outcomes rath|the Universi<br>nts of the a<br>er than spe|ty and the Governing Board shall endeavour to have<br>ccrediting body stated in terms of programme<br>cified curricular content.|\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|**Special Extern**<br>**Examiner**|The special ext<br>Academic Cou<br>School to parti<br>expert in the a|ern examin<br>ncil or its rel<br>cipate in th<br>rea of resea|er is a person who has been approved by the<br>evant committee on the nomination of the Head of<br>e examination of a research degree as a recognised<br>rch of the relevant thesis.|\\n\\n---\\n[File: examination_regulations.md > UCD Examination Regulations >> **5. In-person Examination Regulations**]\\nContent: - who have left an Examination Hall will not be permitted to re-enter.  \\n- **5.5.** Students will not be permitted to leave the Examination Hall during the final ten minutes of the examination period (this facilitates the orderly collection of examination scripts).  \\n- **5.6.** Students may not commence writing until instructed to do so by the Invigilator-in-Charge.  \\n- **5.7.** Students may bring their mobile phone and smartwatch into the Examination Hall but they must be SWITCHED OFF at all times and NOT simply turned to SILENT. These items are to be placed under students’ desks, face up. If any electronic device, including mobile phones / smart watches are found in a POWER ON state or if it rings or sounds an alarm during an examination, the phone or smartwatch will be confiscated for the remainder of the examination and the student will be subject to disciplinary action.\\n\\n---\\n[File: examination_regulations.md > UCD Examination Regulations]\\nContent: **4.4.** During examinations, both in person and online, students should not access any materials other than those specifically authorised by the module coordinator. This includes, but is not limited to, consulting online or hard copies of books, lecture or revision notes, published articles, using internet search engines, pencil cases and most electronic devices, including, but not necessarily limited to, mobile phones and smart watches. Mobile phones and smartwatches must be turned off while in the Examination Centre, or, if they cannot be turned off, they must not be brought into the Examination Centre. Any use of unauthorised materials is a serious breach of discipline. It is important for students to check before an examination and to seek advice if they are unsure about any item in their possession.\\n\\n\\nQuery: Can I get stationery during the exam if I forget to bring my own?\\n\\nAnswer:"}]	"No, you cannot get stationery during the exam if you forget to bring your own. According to UCD Examination Regulations (5.6), students may not commence writing until instructed by the Invigilator-in-Charge. This means that any items brought into the examination hall must be authorized and placed under desks as per regulations, including pencils, pens, erasers, rulers, calculators, etc., unless specifically allowed in advance through a module coordinator.\\n\\nIf you forget to bring your stationery, it is recommended to check with the module coordinator or ask for assistance from the invigilator before entering the examination hall."	DEFAULT	\N	\N	0	0	0	\N	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	2026-07-20 21:00:55.124	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-20 21:01:00.205	\N	\N	\N	\N
