on.\\n\\n---\\n[File: student_academic_misconduct_procedure.md > Student Academic Misconduct Procedure >> **2. Scope**]\\nContent: - Ghost writing  \\n1  \\n---  \\n###### Page 2 of 12  \\nNot all categories of alleged academic misconduct are dealt with by School Academic Integrity Committees. The table below indicates categories of alleged academic misconduct that will be addressed under the Student Discipline Procedure or another designated process.  \\n|**Exam Hall** **Academic Misconduct**|● Invigilator reports of alleged breaches of Examination<br>Regulations should be submitted to be dealt with<br>under the Student Discipline Procedure by<br>Assessment in the case of centrally organised exams<br>and by Module Coordinators in relation to locally<br>organised examinations.|\\n|---|---|\\n\\n---\\n[File: guide_exams_assessment.md > Exams & Assessment]\\nContent: Exams & Assessment\\nHome\\nStudent Guides\\nExams & Assessment\\nExams are a part of university life. UCD Student Advisers know that exams can be stressful for students, and they often require a different set of skills than those learnt at school or work.\\nFor information related to the exam process itself,\\nUCD Assessment\\nis the best place to go for up-to-date information, including how to access your timetable, how to get to the exam centres, and the procedures in place during exams. You will also find useful information on your exam results at this link.\\nPreparing for exams\\nIf you would like some tips on how to improve your study skills and exam techniques then you may find our\\nguide on\\nAcademic Support\\nhelpful\\n.\\nIf you have questions related to your exam or module content, please contact your module coordinator(s).\\nCoping with exam stress\\n\\n---\\n[File: academic_regulations_2025_26.md > **ACADEMIC REGULATIONS 2025-2026** >> Contents]\\nContent: |**Professional**<br>**Accreditation**|The University is responsible for the design and validation of its own degree<br>programmes. Where those programmes are also subject to professional|  \\n9  \\n---  \\n###### Page 10 of 84  \\n||accreditation,<br>the requireme<br>outcomes rath|the Universi<br>nts of the a<br>er than spe|ty and the Governing Board shall endeavour to have<br>ccrediting body stated in terms of programme<br>cified curricular content.|\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n|**Special Extern**<br>**Examiner**|The special ext<br>Academic Cou<br>School to parti<br>expert in the a|ern examin<br>ncil or its rel<br>cipate in th<br>rea of resea|er is a person who has been approved by the<br>evant committee on the nomination of the Head of<br>e examination of a research degree as a recognised<br>rch of the relevant thesis.|\\n\\n---\\n[File: study_and_exam_leave_policy.md > Study and Exam Leave Policy >> **5. Related documents**]\\nContent: Study & Examination Leave Application Form\\n\\n\\nQuery: where can I find the exam TIme table\\n\\nAnswer:"}]	"To find the exam time table, you should refer to:\\n\\n- The University's official website or homepage.\\n- The UCD Assessment page for up-to-date information on exams and assessment procedures.\\n- Contact your module coordinator(s) directly if specific questions arise related to your course."	DEFAULT	\N	\N	56	1026	1082	\N	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	2026-07-20 21:09:22.105	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-20 21:09:24.136	\N	\N	\N	\N
