f64c1811-0bf4-4622-9234-4861b9d0a9a6	2026-07-20 20:48:56.403	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "Hi"}	{"answer": "Hello! 👋\\n\\nI am the UCD Policy Assistant. I can help answer your questions regarding UCD policies. How can I help you today?"}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 20:48:56.9	2026-07-20 20:48:56.906
18fe95f5-e855-4205-bb0c-db9e64e1094f	2026-07-20 20:49:30.806	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "What is the academic centers policy?"}	{"answer": "The Academic Centres Policy outlines how UCD encourages the establishment and governance of Academic Centres. It provides mechanisms for oversight to maintain high standards and structures/processes that facilitate Centre activities. The policy defines an Academic Centre, principles, roles, responsibilities, and establishes processes for approval as an Academic Centre through the Academic Council's delegated authority from the Governing Authority.\\n\\nKey points:\\n- 1.1: Encourages establishment of Academic Centres responding to research/education opportunities and promoting interdisciplinary collaboration.\\n- 1.2: Provides governance and oversight mechanisms with structures/processes that facilitate Centre activities, defines an Academic Centre, principles, roles, responsibilities for establishment, continuation, and review.\\n\\nThe policy also mentions the need for support from Head of School, College Principal, and University Vice-President for Research Innovation and Impact in applications for approval as an Academic Centre.", "citations": [{"title": "employee_code_of_conduct_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "academic_centres_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "academic_integrity_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "statement_on_academic_freedom.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 20:49:31.41	2026-07-20 20:49:37.165
8791b418-d280-4037-8822-189f67b9d427	2026-07-20 20:53:20.55	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "can I bring my phone to the exam?"}	{"answer": "No, you are not permitted to bring your mobile phone into the Examination Hall during an in-person examination as per UCD Examination Regulations. According to **5.7**, students must switch off their mobile phones and smartwatches at all times while in the Examination Hall. If any electronic device is found in a powered-on state or if it rings or sounds an alarm, it will be confiscated for the remainder of the examination and subject to disciplinary action.", "citations": [{"title": "examination_regulations.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "guide_exams_assessment.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "student_code_of_conduct.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 20:53:20.585	2026-07-20 20:53:24.196
f56875f2-6f54-4d08-9f25-71bb4bbdd501	2026-07-20 20:53:49.683	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "what are extenuating Circumstances?"}	{"answer": "**Extenuating Circumstances**\\n\\nExtenuating circumstances refer to serious, unforeseen events that prevent a student from meeting the requirements of their program. These circumstances may include:\\n\\n- Missing an examination or test  \\n- Failing to submit all or any part of continuous assessments by the due date  \\n- Performing below your ability in work submitted or examinations attended  \\n- Circumstances that persisted throughout the trimester or a substantial part of it that affected your performance\\n\\nExamples of extenuating circumstances include:\\n\\n- Involvement in an accident  \\n- Victim of crime  \\n- An acute illness or serious on-going medical condition  \\n- Ongoing life-threatening illness of a close family member or partner  \\n- Bereavement of a close family member or partner  \\n- Acute or on-going serious personal/emotional circumstances  \\n- Domestic upheaval at the time of the assessment (e.g. fire, burglary, eviction)\\n\\nThese circumstances are beyond your control and negatively impact your ability to fully engage with academic requirements. If you have any further questions about how your fees may be affected by this, please contact the Student Desk: ucd.ie/askus.\\n\\n**Note:** Short extensions can be requested via the **UCD Office of Students' Affairs** (https://www.ucd.ie/studentadvisers/studentguides/extenuatingcircumstances/) for up to 10 working days.", "citations": [{"title": "guide_extenuating_circumstances.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "assessment_code_of_practice.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "extenuating_circumstances_student_guide.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "extenuating_circumstances.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 20:53:49.923	2026-07-20 20:53:55.014
a93bd8ae-b91f-4792-9061-7b6a5ab7f23c	2026-07-20 20:54:10.051	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "What are exam rules?"}	{"answer": "Exam Rules:\\n\\n- **6.1** - Students must follow instructions issued by their Module Coordinator or nominee or invigilator.\\n- **6.2** - Students should log in at least 15 minutes before the commencement of each assessment.\\n- **6.3** - Students should ensure that the space to be used for taking the examination is as quiet as possible and free from likely disruptions.\\n- **6.4** - Students should ensure that the chair/desk is comfortable, there is adequate lighting, space, and refreshments available if needed.\\n- **6.5** - All devices not required for taking the exam should be turned off.\\n- **6.6** - Students are to use a computer rather than a mobile or tablet device to take the examination; UCD Library provides a laptop loan service when necessary.\\n\\nThese rules aim to ensure that students have a fair and conducive environment during exams, maintaining academic integrity and fairness in assessment practices.", "citations": [{"title": "guide_exams_assessment.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "research_degree_examination_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "examination_regulations.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "assessment_code_of_practice.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 20:54:10.153	2026-07-20 20:54:14.73
4587c4e5-c070-4554-b222-7e2498797d4a	2026-07-20 20:54:25.392	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "What is the weather today?"}	{"answer": "The provided context does not contain any information about the current weather. Therefore, I must state explicitly that the answer is:\\n\\nThe weather cannot be determined from the given context.", "citations": [{"title": "overtime_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "short_term_unpaid_leave_policy_staff_on_probation.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "how_to_submit_a_document.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "research_degree_examination_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "employment_contract_management_policy_post_doctoral_research_staff_humanities_an.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 20:54:25.837	2026-07-20 20:54:27.367
7b82b36e-dcbe-4866-9025-0f5a56687088	2026-07-20 21:00:54.447	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "Can I get stationery during the exam if I forget to bring my own?"}	{"answer": "No, you cannot get stationery during the exam if you forget to bring your own. According to UCD Examination Regulations (5.6), students may not commence writing until instructed by the Invigilator-in-Charge. This means that any items brought into the examination hall must be authorized and placed under desks as per regulations, including pencils, pens, erasers, rulers, calculators, etc., unless specifically allowed in advance through a module coordinator.\\n\\nIf you forget to bring your stationery, it is recommended to check with the module coordinator or ask for assistance from the invigilator before entering the examination hall.", "citations": [{"title": "examination_regulations.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "guide_exams_assessment.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "academic_regulations_2025_26.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 21:00:54.583	2026-07-20 21:01:00.199
6c9b82a4-da97-4458-8090-f0e0ce2a5678	2026-07-20 21:08:34.039	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "where can I find the exam time table"}	{"answer": "To find the exam timetable, you should visit the following link:\\n\\n- Exams & Assessment > Home > Student Guides > Exams & Assessment > Exams are a part of university life. UCD Student Advisers know that exams can be stressful for students, and they often require a different set of skills than those learnt at school or work.\\n\\nYou will find useful information on your exam results at this link:\\n\\n- Exams & Assessment > Home > Student Guides > Exams & Assessment > Coping with exam stress\\n\\nAdditionally, you may want to check the following pages for more detailed information:\\n\\n- Exams & Assessment > Home > Student Guides > Exams & Assessment > Preparing for exams\\n- Exams & Assessment > Home > Student Guides > Exams & Assessment > Exams are a part of university life. UCD Student Advisers know that exams can be stressful for students, and they often require a different set of skills than those learnt at school or work.\\n\\nFor more information on your exam results:\\n\\n- Exams & Assessment > Home > Student Guides > Exams & Assessment > Coping with exam stress\\n\\nIf you have questions related to your exam or module content, please contact your module coordinator(s).", "citations": [{"title": "examination_regulations.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "overtime_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "guide_exams_assessment.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "assessment_code_of_practice.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 21:08:34.511	2026-07-20 21:08:43.729
2163ce85-88aa-4279-a9d1-bd4bf39ea916	2026-07-20 21:09:21.435	chat_response	cmrtp2m3m000610fjbampscbo	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	{"question": "where can I find the exam TIme table"}	{"answer": "To find the exam time table, you should refer to:\\n\\n- The University's official website or homepage.\\n- The UCD Assessment page for up-to-date information on exams and assessment procedures.\\n- Contact your module coordinator(s) directly if specific questions arise related to your course.", "citations": [{"title": "assessment_code_of_practice.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "student_academic_misconduct_procedure.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "guide_exams_assessment.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "academic_regulations_2025_26.md", "source_url": "#"}, {"title": "study_and_exam_leave_policy.md", "source_url": "#"}]}	\N	{}	2026-07-20 21:09:21.573	2026-07-20 21:09:24.133
